-- 031: updated profile write-up for the Publicity Secretary (Counsel Moses Omara).
-- Replaces the biography only; his photograph, title and role description are not touched.

UPDATE leaders SET
  bio = 'Counsel Moses Omara is a Ugandan Advocate of the High Court of Uganda and a legal practitioner with professional experience in public institutional governance, legal advisory services, litigation and case management, statutory and regulatory compliance, contract drafting and review, and administrative law. He holds a Bachelor of Laws degree from Gulu University, a Postgraduate Diploma in Legal Practice from the Law Development Centre, and a Master of Laws degree from IPSK.

Moses has served at Gulu University for over six years, progressing from Assistant Legal Officer to Legal Officer. In this capacity, he has provided legal advisory services to University Management, Senate, the Appointments Board and various committees of the University Council. His professional responsibilities encompass institutional legal advisory services, litigation management, contract review, recruitment and disciplinary proceedings, statutory compliance, and strengthening institutional governance. He has particularly contributed to streamlining the composition and membership of Senate and its committees in accordance with the applicable legal framework, as well as promoting procedural fairness, accountability and adherence to the principles of natural justice in institutional decision-making.

Beyond his institutional responsibilities, Counsel Omara serves as the inaugural Publicity Secretary of the Gulu University Convocation (GUCO), having been sworn into office on 5th November 2024 at Gulu University Main Campus. As a member of the Convocation Executive Committee, he plays an important role in member mobilisation, information dissemination, public engagement, social media and website management, and stakeholder relations. He contributes to strengthening the visibility and institutional identity of the Convocation, fostering connections among Gulu University alumni, and promoting initiatives that enhance the University''s reputation and engagement with its wider community.

Moses has also participated in national-level legal and higher education governance initiatives. He served as Chairperson of the Technical Committee of the Vice Chancellors'' Forum under the Higher Education Management Information Systems (HEMIS) Consortium, which was responsible for drafting and finalising the Academic Management Information System (ACMIS) Memorandum of Understanding. He has further served on various institutional investigation, disciplinary and policy review committees.

His broader professional engagements include legal research, community mediation, human rights advocacy, environmental and natural-resource governance, constitutionalism and public accountability. He has previously worked with the Acholi Religious Leaders Peace Initiative, the Inter-Religious Council of Uganda and other community-based justice and development initiatives.

Counsel Omara is passionate about the rule of law, institutional accountability, access to justice, good governance, alumni engagement and the effective administration of public institutions. His professional philosophy is anchored in integrity, impartiality, responsible leadership, analytical legal reasoning and the conviction that law should serve as an instrument for justice, institutional development and societal transformation.

Through his professional practice, institutional leadership and service to the Gulu University Convocation, he remains committed to advancing legal excellence, strengthening public institutions and building meaningful bridges between the University, its alumni and the wider community.'
WHERE organ = 'executive' AND title = 'Publicity Secretary' AND name = 'Counsel Moses Omara';
